OL,3,ARoofing scammers con homeowners out of
OL,4,Athousands of pounds
OL,5,
OL,6,FScammers pretending to be legitimate
OL,7,Fworkmen are charging homeowners
OL,8,Fthousands of pounds for roofing work
OL,9,Fthat is not completed, done badly or
OL,10,Fnot necessary, according to Citizens
OL,11,FAdvice.
OL,13,FThe consumer advice charity says one in
OL,14,F10 of all the scams it recorded over
OL,15,Fthe past year were related to roofing,
OL,16,Fmaking it the most common type of scam
OL,17,Fbrought to them.
OL,19,FIt can leave victims like Crystal, from
OL,20,Fthe Midlands, thousands of pounds out
OL,21,Fof pocket.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
